    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed anchor. His score of 87.14 is the highest on the slate, fueled by a high-value matchup against Lowder and, crucially, the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a massive boost to our team\u2019s priority on stolen bases. Joining him at the top of the projected output is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who benefits from a significant park factor and a platoon advantage that pushes him into \"Strong\" territory. While **Gabriel Moreno** (70.02) also draws a favorable look against Lowder, keep a close eye on the 45% rain risk impacting **Mickey Moniak** and **Travis Bazzana**; if the weather clears, their aggressive park-adjusted projections make them potential league-winners for today\u2019s scoring window.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range, where **Josh Naylor** (58.13) narrowly edged out **Max Muncy** (48.80) to capture the final spot. While **Max Muncy** carries upside, his projected spot at the bottom of the order and the lack of a strong platoon advantage pushed him below the utility floor compared to **Josh Naylor**\u2019s more consistent lineup placement. We also opted to sit **Jose Caballero** (39.32), whose sub-40 efficiency score was non-negotiable despite his stolen base utility; facing an elite arm like Cease in a neutral-to-bad platoon environment makes him too high-risk for a roster aiming to maintain daily efficiency. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a \"Strong\" play despite a mediocre SP matchup, as his dynamic platoon advantage provides enough cushion to keep him in the 1B slot over our deeper bench options.",
